{% set local_problem %}
<p>New Market properties face a drainage dilemma: no municipal storm drains, but plenty of water to manage. Surface extensions only move water a few feet before releasing it onto clay soil that doesn't absorb much.</p>

<p>The advantage of rural property? Space. You have room to route water properly — not just a few feet from your foundation, but 20, 30, or 50+ feet to a location where it can't cause problems.</p>

<p>Underground drains make this possible. They capture roof runoff and move it through buried pipes to discharge points you choose — low spots, drainage areas, or simply far enough away that it disperses naturally.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drains are buried pipes connecting downspouts to discharge points. Water flows through sealed channels to pop-up emitters, dry wells, or daylight exits far from your home.</p>

<p>We design systems for your specific property — routing around obstacles, matching terrain, and using your available space effectively.</p>

<p>For New Market properties without municipal drainage, underground systems often make more sense than elaborate surface extensions. You have the room — we help you use it.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been installing underground drainage in north Madison County for over 20 years. We understand rural properties without city infrastructure and design accordingly.</p>

<p>Our systems last decades. Quality materials, proper installation, and thoughtful design mean permanent solutions.</p>
{% endset %}
